      "notation": "round-trip-adjudicator",
      "description": "Rules on a translation round trip: given the source strings and the back-translation, and never the target text, it pre-screens every pair mechanically, reads each flagged pair in full, and records drift or not-drift for each with the reason. A specialisation of `adjudicator` for the translation instance of untainted verification; it adds the translation-specific drift definition.",
